
{"id":"aeef14ab-2d0f-4ab7-9a9d-75747c37004c","object":"chat.completion","created":1785002539,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes=case['nodes']\\n    req=set(case['required_symbols'])\\n    by_id={n['id']:n for n in nodes}\\n    retain=set()\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if not n['removable']:\\n            retain.add(n['id'])\\n    covered={n['symbol'] for n in nodes if n['id'] in retain and n['symbol'] in req}\\n    missing=req-covered\\n    if missing:\\n        cands=[n for n in nodes if n['removable'] and n['symbol'] in missing]\\n        cands.sort(key=lambda n:(-n['utility'], n['id']))\\n        used=set()\\n        for n in cands:\\n            if n['symbol'] in missing and n['symbol'] not in used:\\n                retain.add(n['id'])\\n                used.add(n['symbol'])\\n    removed=[n['id'] for n in nodes if n['id'] not in retain]\\n    retained=[n['id'] for n in nodes if n['id'] in retain]\\n    return {'removed_node_ids':removed,'retained_node_ids':retained}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to understand the task: SE-PE-01. The payload contains nodes with id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility. And required_symbols. We need to produce removed_node_ids and retained_node_ids.\n\nFrom the description: \"grammar_guided_node_reduction\" but we only have a tree with nodes, not a grammar. However, the problem seems related to removing nodes that are \"removable\" while preserving required_symbols and possibly maximizing utility? The public fixture shows three similar cases. The expected behavior is not explicitly given, but we need to infer the algorithm from the phrase \"grammar_guided_node_reduction\" and \"bounded objective: Reduce a registered parse tree through grammar-valid deletion and replacement candidates while preserving an interestingness oracle.\"\n\nGiven the structure: nodes form a tree via parent references. Some nodes a